---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import OnThisPage from '../components/OnThisPage.astro';
import DayStop from '../components/DayStop.astro';
import Kiosk from '../components/Kiosk.astro';
import TriageBoard from '../components/TriageBoard.astro';
import DeviceRace from '../components/DeviceRace.astro';
import DoctorFlow from '../components/DoctorFlow.astro';
import FloorClock from '../components/FloorClock.astro';
import FloorMap from '../components/FloorMap.astro';
import NightlyReport from '../components/NightlyReport.astro';
import Changed from '../components/Changed.astro';
import HowIWork from '../components/HowIWork.astro';
import BeforeThis from '../components/BeforeThis.astro';
import Questions from '../components/Questions.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';
---
<Base>
  <Hero />
  <OnThisPage />

  <!-- The spine: one clinic day in seven parts, each with a recreation of the real screen. -->
  <div id="day" style="scroll-margin-top: var(--bar-h)">

    <DayStop id="checkin" n={1} time="Early morning · front desk" title="Patients check themselves in, and their chart stays up to date on its own." next={{ id: 'boards', label: 'A screen for every role' }}>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <p class="body">
          Patients place their health card or licence in a reader at the desk. The kiosk greets them by
          name, asks whether their details are still right, and marks them as arrived. If something on
          the card has changed, the chart is brought up to date for them.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          The front desk is free to actually greet people instead of typing, and older patients manage
          it on their own, because there is nothing to type or search.
        </p>
        <div class="fact"><b>Checking in takes one tap, and the front desk does nothing.</b><span>In use at the clinic's front desk since September 2026, with a touch option for anyone without a card.</span></div>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="visual">
        <Kiosk />
        <p class="screen-cap">The kiosk's own wording, screen by screen. It keeps cycling on its own.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </DayStop>

    <DayStop id="boards" n={2} time="Mid-morning · every screen in the clinic" title="Every screen in the clinic shows who is next, so nobody has to go looking." flip next={{ id: 'devices', label: 'Test results into the chart' }}>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <p class="body">
          Each role has its own screen, built around what that person needs to know. Doctors see who is
          ready for them and for how long. The imaging tech sees who is next for a scan and which room is
          open. The front desk sees who has arrived and who is running late.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          When someone moves a patient along on their screen, every other screen follows, and the
          patient's status in the EMR is kept in step. Nobody writes the same thing down twice.
        </p>
        <div class="fact"><b>One screen for each role, all showing the same picture.</b><span>Doctors can open theirs on a phone between rooms.</span></div>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="visual">
        <TriageBoard />
        <ul class="tb-roles" aria-label="who sees what">
          <li><i style="background:var(--s-purple)"></i><span><b>Doctors:</b> who is ready for them, longest wait first.</span></li>
          <li><i style="background:var(--s-yellow)"></i><span><b>Imaging:</b> who is next for a scan, and which room is open.</span></li>
          <li><i style="background:var(--s-orange)"></i><span><b>Testing rooms:</b> the same, for those stations.</span></li>
          <li><i style="background:var(--s-green)"></i><span><b>Front desk:</b> who has arrived, and who needs a hand.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </Fragment>
    </DayStop>

    <DayStop id="devices" n={3} time="Late morning · imaging room" title="Test results make their way into the chart without anyone typing them." next={{ id: 'doctor', label: "The doctor's room" }}>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <p class="body">
          Most clinic machines print a slip or save a file, and then someone copies the numbers into the
          chart by hand. It is slow, it happens all day long, and now and then a digit slips.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          Here, the machine's results reach the patient's chart on their own, moments after the test,
          exactly as measured. The tech carries on to the next patient.
        </p>
        <div class="fact"><b>Results land in the chart in about half a second, instead of a couple of minutes of typing.</b><span>Running at the clinic since May 2026, with nothing to catch or correct.</span></div>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="visual">
        <DeviceRace />
      </Fragment>
    </DayStop>

    <DayStop id="doctor" n={4} time="Late morning · exam room" title="When the doctor walks in, everything about the patient is already open." flip next={{ id: 'staff', label: 'Schedules and the time clock' }}>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <p class="body">
          A doctor usually needs the chart, the scans and the photos before an exam can start, and they
          live in different programs. Finding the right patient in each one takes a little time, every
          single visit.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          Now the doctor taps the patient's name once on the lounge screen. The chart opens on one
          monitor, and the scans and photos open side by side on the other, already on the right patient
          and the right view for that visit.
        </p>
        <div class="fact"><b>Everything open in a few seconds, from one tap.</b><span>Down from about half a minute of searching for each patient.</span></div>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="visual">
        <DoctorFlow />
      </Fragment>
    </DayStop>

    <DayStop id="staff" n={5} time="Midday · staff room" title="The manager's week, the schedule and the time clock, all from one screen." next={{ id: 'map', label: 'A live map of the clinic' }}>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <p class="body">
          The paper sheet showing who is at which station became a screen in the staff room. The manager
          changes it from the office, and everyone sees the change at once.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          Staff clock in and out on the same screen with a personal code. The manager gets a short
          summary in the morning and at the end of the day, and the pay-period timesheet arrives ready
          to go, with the totals already done.
        </p>
        <div class="fact"><b>No more paper sheet, punch clock, or adding up hours by hand.</b><span>In use since the end of September 2026.</span></div>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="visual">
        <FloorClock />
        <p class="screen-cap">The staff-room screen, with the time clock built in. The names are made up.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </DayStop>

    <DayStop id="map" n={6} time="Afternoon · anywhere in the clinic" title="A live map of the day, so staff can see the whole clinic at a glance." flip next={{ id: 'nightly', label: 'Looking back on the day' }}>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <p class="body">
          The same information that drives the screens also draws a simple map of the clinic. Each
          patient is a dot that moves from the front desk, through testing and imaging, into an exam
          room and out, changing colour as they go.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          It is a small thing, and the staff like it. It is also the quickest way to notice a room
          sitting empty while people are waiting.
        </p>
        <div class="fact"><b>The whole clinic, in one glance.</b><span>The colours match the screens, so everyone reads it the same way.</span></div>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="visual">
        <FloorMap />
        <p class="screen-cap">Made-up patients, moving the way a real day does.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </DayStop>

    <DayStop id="nightly" n={7} time="After close" title="Overnight, the day is looked over so tomorrow runs a little smoother." next={{ id: 'changed', label: 'What changed' }}>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <p class="body">
          Everything that happens on the screens is remembered with a time, without anyone writing it
          down. After close, the day is reviewed: where people waited longest, which rooms sat quiet while
          others were waiting, and what helped.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          The clinic gets a short note in plain language before the first patient arrives. Over time the
          suggestions get better at reflecting how your clinic actually runs. The staff always make the
          final call.
        </p>
        <div class="fact"><b>A short note each morning on where yesterday slowed down, and what to try.</b><span>Built from the day's own record, not from anyone's memory.</span></div>
      </Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="visual">
        <NightlyReport />
        <p class="screen-cap">An example note, in the shape of the real one. The numbers change every day.</p>
      </Fragment>
    </DayStop>
  </div>

  <Changed />
  <HowIWork />
  <BeforeThis />
  <Questions />
  <Contact />
</Base>
